sdl2: keep the window's size when the guest catches up after full screen

Applies on top of 0028.

The guest takes the size the window gives it a second or more later. When
the window left full screen before the guest had switched to the full
screen size, the guest switched to it afterwards, and sdl2_window_resize
sized the window to it: the guest's full screen size plus a frame, larger
than the work area. That size also became SDL's windowed size, so later
rounds of full screen came back to it. A busy guest can also be a round
behind: after the window left full screen it showed the windowed size of
the round before, then this round's full screen size.

The sizes a window has while full screen are now remembered from SDL's
resize events. After the window leaves full screen it does not follow the
guest to one of them unless it is the size the window asks the guest for
now, until the user asks for the guest's size with Ctrl+Alt+0 or the window
goes full screen again.

Ctrl+Alt+F switches only the window it is pressed in, while gui_fullscreen
is shared by every window, so it now goes by that window's own state;
with two displays started full screen the second window's first press
did nothing. A window remembers its own full screen size when it enters and
leaves full screen, a window created again starts clean, and a display
without ui-info, which is never asked for a size, does not hold back.

